# The directory Mix will write compiled artifacts to.
/_build/

# If you run "mix test --cover", coverage assets end up here.
/cover/

# The directory Mix downloads your dependencies sources to.
/deps/

# Ignore .fetch files in case you like to edit your project deps locally.
/.fetch

# If the VM crashes, it generates a dump, let's ignore it too.
erl_crash.dump

# Also ignore archive artifacts (built via "mix archive.build").
*.ez

# Temporary files, for example, from tests.
/tmp/

# Local backup namespaces -- never commit. TWO mechanisms live here with
# DIFFERENT retention rules, each confined to its own directory so that a sweep
# of one cannot reach the other's artefacts (D35, dc 2026-08-15):
#
#   .backup/upgrade/<UTC>/        rollback artefacts from `intent upgrade`
#   .backup/db/<tier>/<UTC>.db    rolling DB snapshots; tier = daily|weekly|monthly
#
# The namespace is a DIRECTORY rather than a filename prefix on purpose: it makes
# the filesystem enforce the separation instead of every future glob having to be
# written correctly. NOTHING ever sweeps `.backup/` root, so `backup-<TS>/`
# directories predating this layout stay there untouched and permanently safe.
/.backup/

# Per-developer Claude Code permissions (paths and tool allowlist vary by user).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Backup and editor scratch files, as a CLASS.
#
# An ignore rule naming an exact filename never covers that file's backups, and
# this repository is PUBLIC (`gh repo view --json visibility` -> PUBLIC), so an
# unignored backup is one `git add -A` away from being world-readable and
# permanently in a history nobody can rewrite. Four concurrent sessions share
# this working tree and the `-A` hazard has already fired here once.
#
# This project has patched this exact class one filename at a time before --
# the line here used to read `/AGENTS.md.bak`, and `.claude/settings.local.json`
# above is ignored while `.claude/settings.local.json.bak` was not. Both are
# covered by the class rule, so the single-filename rule is pruned rather than
# left beside it (Highlander: one rule for one concern).
*.bak
*.orig
*~
*.swp

# Ignore package tarball (built via "mix hex.build").
multiplyer-*.tar

# Ignore assets that are produced by build tools.
/priv/static/assets/

# Ignore digested assets cache.
/priv/static/cache_manifest.json

# In case you use Node.js/npm, you want to ignore these.
npm-debug.log
/assets/node_modules/

# Nonsense macOS gumpf 
.DS_Store

# No need to check in .obsidian files
.obsidian

# *.beams
*.beam

# Never check in secrets 
/config/*.secret.exs

# ElixirLS no no no
.elixir_ls/

# The v3 SQLite db. NOT disposable, NOT derived, and NOT "never truth" -- hv
# reversed D01 on 2026-08-15: the SQLite db is the DURABLE SSOT and everything on
# disk is a secondary artefact. The three claims this comment used to make are
# all false and are deleted rather than reworded.
#
# RULED (D34, hv, 2026-08-15): the DB is per-machine truth and is NEVER
# committed. Truth TRAVELS as the lossless .json/.md extract, and a fresh clone
# reconstitutes its DB by passing that extract through the intentsvcs ingest
# gate. So the ignore is correct -- on the ceiling, not on binary-merge folklore:
# git delta-compresses SQLite well, but FTS5 expansion is ~1.95x and GitHub hard-
# blocks at 100 MB, which a whole-project corpus crosses.
#
# THAT 1.95x HAS A PENDING FALSIFIER, PAIRED WITH ISSUE 0029 (vc, 2026-08-15).
# 0029 proposes contentless FTS5 -- `doc_sections` declares no `content=`, so it
# stores a verbatim second copy of every file's text -- which roughly halves the
# DB and takes the ratio to ~0.70x. If 0029 lands this number is FALSE, sitting
# in a comment that reads as settled measurement and justifying a rule that stays
# correct for a reason that has changed. That is the D29 shape arriving through
# the fix rather than through the original. 0029 carries "update this ratio" as
# part of its fix; this note is the other end, because a cross-reference written
# at one end only is not a pairing. The CONCLUSION does NOT move either way:
# ~29.6 MB still stays well out of git, so 0029 does not reopen D34.
#
# THIS IS A PATH RULE AND DELIBERATELY NOT A CLASS RULE. There is no `*.db` line
# here and there should not be: now that the DB is durable truth, a blanket glob
# would assert a durability policy about a whole class for every consumer of this
# file. The one instance is named because `Project::db_path()` resolves exactly
# one location (`project.rs:302`) -- but `Store::open()` takes a path PARAMETER,
# so this list can never be exhaustive by construction. The class-wide protection
# is a REFUSAL in `bin/int precommit`, not a wider glob here: an ignore silently
# hides the paths it knows, whereas the guard blocks the ones it does not.
#
# `intent/.cache/` remains a name that contradicts the model -- a directory
# called `.cache` holding durable truth keeps telling readers it is disposable,
# which is what made the old comment here natural to write. cc's under D21.
#
# Kept for the reason it was added, which is unaffected: the database was showing
# as `?? intent/.cache/` -- one `git add -A` from entering history as a binary
# blob. Also the precondition for D29: the ingest corpus
# excludes IGNORED paths, so until this line existed the DB was outside the corpus
# only by accident of path shape.
intent/.cache/

# `intent/.backup/` -- the SAME defect as the line above, in the sibling
# directory, found the first time anyone actually ran `intent backup` on the
# hoisted repo (cc, 2026-08-18). `/.backup/` at line 33 is ANCHORED TO THE REPO
# ROOT and v3 writes snapshots to `intent/.backup/db/<UTC>.db`, so the rule and
# the tool disagreed about the path and the rule silently covered nothing.
#
# **NOT because it would otherwise reach history.** `bin/.devbin/cmd/precommit`
# refuses a staged `*.db`/`-wal`/`-shm`/`*.sqlite` by name AND by SQLite magic
# under a name that does not say so, which is the class-wide protection this
# file's own comment points at. That guard holds.
#
# It is here for the second reason the block above gives, which is the
# load-bearing one: **D29's precondition.** The ingest corpus excludes IGNORED
# paths, so until this line existed a snapshot of the store sat INSIDE the
# corpus the store is built from -- and the only thing keeping it out was the
# accident that nobody had taken a backup yet.
intent/.backup/
target/
# The DDL face is a COMMITTED artefact (the global gitignore excludes *.sql).
!schema/ddl.sql

# D53: the event log lives in the store; its file form is produced by `intent export`.
intent/events.jsonl

# The critic gate is SHIPPED CANON, installed by `intent claude upgrade` into
# whatever `git rev-parse --git-path hooks` resolves to -- which is this tracked
# directory once core.hooksPath is set. Tracking it would be a SECOND HOME FOR
# CANON, which is the class this repository spent 2026-08-20 removing from the
# guard roster. The installer owns this file; git must not.
.githooks/pre-commit.intent
